			</attacks>
			<backstory><![CDATA[Ursa Catchum’s Short Backstory:

Ursa Catchum grew up in the forests near Eldridge Village as the son of the legendary wildfire druid, Ash Catchum. From a young age, Ursa was taught the ways of the Circle of the Eternal Stars, a druidic order that drew power from the constellations. His father often shared the mysteries of nature and the stars, fostering Ursa’s curiosity and magic.

When Ursa was four, his father disappeared while investigating strange planar disturbances, leaving behind a legacy of unanswered questions. After Ash's disappearance, the Circle of the Eternal Stars took Ursa under their wing, helping him grow as a druid. At age six, Ursa developed the Dragonmark of Handling, giving him a special bond with magical creatures.

Ursa now carries three enchanted potatoes—powerful magical items once held by his father’s adventuring party. He joins Lilly Glimmergear and Stabby Sharpblade on a quest to uncover the truth behind the planar disturbances, his father’s fate, and the mysteries of the enchanted potatoes. Guided by the stars, Ursa is determined to follow in his father’s footsteps and find the answers he seeks.You come from a humble social rank, but you are destined for so much more. Already the people of your home village regard you as their champion, and your destiny calls you to stand against the tyrants and monsters that threaten the common folk everywhere.]]></backstory>
			<background-trinket>Three Enchanted Potatoes</background-trinket>
			<background-traits>Determined and Resilient: Though young, Ursa is determined to find out what happened to his father and to uncover the truth behind the enchanted potatoes. He doesn’t give up easily, even when faced with challenges. "I won’t stop until I find the answers."If someone is in trouble, I’m always ready to lend help.</background-traits>
			<background-ideals>Fate and Destiny: He believes that the stars guide the destinies of individuals and that his path is part of a greater cosmic plan. "The stars have written my path, and I will follow it."</background-ideals>
			<background-bonds>Lilly and Stabby: Ursa is fiercely loyal to his friends, Lilly and Stabby. They are his new family, and he is devoted to their shared journey. "Together, we will uncover the truth and face whatever dangers come our way."</background-bonds>
			<background-flaws>Fear of Failure: Deep down, Ursa fears that he may not be able to live up to his father’s legacy or solve the mysteries surrounding the potatoes. This fear can make him hesitate or push himself too hard, leading to mistakes. "What if I’m not strong enough to do what he couldn’t?"</background-flaws>
			<background>
				<feature name="Animal Whisperer">
					<description><![CDATA[Due to his Dragonmark of Handling, Ursa can communicate with beasts more easily than others. He can understand their emotions and desires, often calming or befriending them in dangerous situations. This gives him an edge in dealing with magical or wild creatures, as he can soothe them with relative ease.]]></description>
				</feature>
			</background>
			<organization>
				<name>Circle of the Eternal Stars</name>
				<symbol>C:\Users\jhffm\OneDrive\Documents\5e Character Builder\gallery\symbols\circle of the eternal starscircle of the eternal stars symbol.png</symbol>
				<allies><![CDATA[Ursa Catchum’s allies are:
Lilly Glimmergear – A 7-year-old svirfneblin artificer and close friend. Her inventive mind complements Ursa’s druidic powers, and they share a strong bond.
Stabby Sharpblade – An 8-year-old goblin monk, fiercely loyal and a chaotic but skilled ally in combat.
Ash Catchum (In Spirit) – Ursa’s missing father, whose memory and teachings guide Ursa on his quest.
The Circle of the Eternal Stars – Ursa’s druidic order, who taught him the ways of the stars and nature, offering guidance from afar.]]></allies>
			</organization>
			<additional-features><![CDATA[1. Star-Guided
Celestial Navigation: Ursa can use the stars to find his way, even in unfamiliar or difficult terrain. When the stars are visible, Ursa can always determine his position and the direction he needs to travel.
Predict Celestial Events: Ursa can predict significant celestial events, such as eclipses or meteor showers, days in advance. This allows him to prepare for potential magical or natural shifts tied to these events.
2. Creature Whisperer
Dragonmark of Handling: Ursa’s Dragonmark allows him to communicate with animals and magical creatures more easily, understanding their emotions and needs. He can calm creatures, befriend them, or gain insight into their behavior.
Bond with Magical Creatures: Due to his Dragonmark, Ursa has an innate ability to form bonds with magical creatures, allowing him to connect with them on a deeper level and sometimes influence their actions.
3. Natural Resilience
Druidic Connection: Ursa’s deep bond with nature grants him resilience in natural environments. He is able to endure harsh weather conditions, quickly find food or shelter, and survive in the wilderness with ease.
Star-Linked Magic: Ursa’s druidic powers are enhanced by the stars. At night, his connection to celestial magic is stronger, allowing him to perform more potent spells when the stars are visible.]]></additional-features>
